// The Observatory (Observatory_2; bible 7.3 step 6, 9). The frame of the shattered Atlas, and the choice. The frame
// offers only the endings Wren has earned (Endings.IsOpen); the Rest is offered in the Blank, at Corvin's chair.
// Unlabelled in-game. The Fixed World: the stones in. The Open World: the frame broken, Runa's chorus, the Complete
// Survey (6.15), and one flight. The Unwritten: Teodor names the places as he lets them go. Voss's coda follows any.

title: Observatory_Frame
---
<<if flag("ending.chosen") > 0>>
    Frame: The frame, as she left it. #still #line:07a43f8
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if not has_flag("act3.started")>>
    Frame: The dome is shut. #still #line:033af0e
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Frame: The frame of the Great Atlas. Seven sockets, brass, a compass rose in each. #still #line:0b777af
Frame: One socket is full. The Observatory's own stone has not left it in forty-one years. #still #line:0690ecb
<<if not ending_open("fixed") and not ending_open("open") and not ending_open("unwritten")>>
    Frame: She stands at it a long time. Not yet. She doesn't know yet what she would do with it. #still #line:0eddeee
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
-> Remake it. All seven. <<if ending_open("fixed")>> #line:0b5efd2
    <<flag ending.chosen 1>>
    <<jump Ending_Fixed>>
-> Break it. Give them back. <<if ending_open("open")>> #line:01a257f
    <<flag ending.chosen 2>>
    <<jump Observatory_Runa_Chorus>>
-> Teodor. They're yours to let go. <<if ending_open("unwritten")>> #line:04c690d
    <<flag ending.chosen 3>>
    <<jump Observatory_Teodor_Unwritten>>
===

title: Ending_Fixed
---
Frame: She sets them in, one by one. Aury's. Hollowvein's. The House's. The hearth's. Isolde's. Corvin's. #line:04752a4
Frame: The seventh socket closes. The Atlas is whole. #line:08c0e86
Frame: Across Aurenne, nothing fades. The Remnant come back in colour, blinking. #line:0557d8e
Frame: Nobody flies. The sky is in the Atlas, held, safe, for everyone. #line:097183d
<<flag ending.fixed 1>>
<<epilogue>>
===

title: Observatory_Runa_Chorus
---
Runa: Break it, then. And sing. Nobody holds the Blank alone. Nobody holds anything alone. #line:06334e9
Runa: Everyone she's met. In order. Here we go. #line:0fc9797
<<sing chorus>>
<<if has_flag("saltmarrow.sable.talked")>>
    Runa: Sable, of the quay, who rows for free. #line:0809b7f
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("saltmarrow.dotha.met")>>
    Runa: Dotha, of Merrow's End, nine songs of eleven. #line:0d06500
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("emberdown.kettil.met")>>
    Runa: Kettil, who counts. Mother. #line:05c2737
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("verdance.teodor.met")>>
    Runa: Teodor, who lets go. #line:09dee41
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("halden.hall.pell_minder")>>
    Runa: Pell, who writes it down. #line:06bd836
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("windreach.idrenne.met")>>
    Runa: Idrenne, who walks. #line:07b81f2
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("blank.ilse.heard")>>
    Runa: Ilse, of the Hollow. #line:089865e
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("corra.decided")>>
    Runa: Corra, who draws. #line:0401ca3
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("return.voss.met")>>
    Runa: Aurelian, at the line. #line:013663b
<<endif>>
Runa: Forty-two, Wren. Isolde. And whoever's in there. #line:0732514
Runa: Now walk it. The whole white. We'll keep singing till you're round. #line:01ccd90
<<flag ending.chorus_led 1>>
Frame: The Atlas stirs in its frame. It wants her on the page. #line:0edb2f6
===

title: Ending_Open_After
---
<<if not has_flag("boss.complete_survey.defeated")>>
    Frame: The Atlas pulls at her, page by page. The singing holds her feet. #still #line:0601e1f
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("ending.open")>>
    Frame: The empty frame. Birds on the rail, trying their wings. #still #line:056f4f6
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Frame: The frame breaks. The stones go home, each carried by whoever lives there. #line:0902c8f
Frame: The Blank folds in. The faded come back grey, and the colour comes over years. #line:021e252
Frame: Anchoring stops working. So does fading. Birds begin, awkwardly, to remember. #line:0659b96
Frame: At the very end, from the Observatory's rail, Wren flies. Once. Briefly. #line:0ae5add
<<grant Sky>>
<<flag ending.open 1>>
<<epilogue>>
===

title: Observatory_Teodor_Unwritten
---
Teodor: May I? Thank you, cartographer. I will name them. They are not gone. They are let go. #line:01e55ab
<<if has_flag("keystone.hollowvein")>>
    Teodor: Hollowvein is. #line:0598941
<<endif>>
Teodor: Aldermere is. #line:00a1b76
<<if place_fate("Saltmarrow_B") == "released">>
    Teodor: Merrow's End is. #line:0065413
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("keystone.quiet_house")>>
    Teodor: The Quiet House is. #line:0c2ad18
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("keystone.windreach")>>
    Teodor: The Steppe is. #line:03d4b6f
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("keystone.aury")>>
    Teodor: Aury's light is. #line:040e916
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("keystone.isolde")>>
    Teodor: Thessaly Hollow is. #line:02794ba
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("keystone.archivist")>>
    Teodor: The old capital is. #line:0108311
<<endif>>
Teodor: There. Now nothing is held. #line:0a9f36c
Frame: Anchoring ends. Fading goes on. The world shrinks to what is lived in, walked, and named. #line:0365b06
<<flag ending.unwritten 1>>
<<epilogue>>
===

title: Observatory_Voss
---
<<if flag("ending.chosen") == 0>>
    Frame: The Guildmaster's chair, empty. His lance against the wall. #line:08a66f7
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("voss.changed")>>
    Voss: Gone in to find her. Hold nothing for me. A. V. #line:0d1c7fb
    Frame: The note is on his desk, in his exact hand, under the small drawing. #line:0c2ff7c
<<else>>
    Frame: A statue at the Observatory door that was not there before. #line:0602b79
    Frame: A grey heron in brass, facing the Greyfold. Nobody remembers commissioning it. #line:01ec81f
<<endif>>
<<flag ending.voss_coda 1>>
===
